## Fonts and UI libraries — vendored (self-hosted, no CDN)

The app loads nothing from a third-party origin. These four were the last
cross-origin subresources and are now committed here, each with its upstream
license text alongside it:

- `vendor/fonts/` — **Orbitron** (v35, © The Orbitron Project Authors) and
  **VT323** (v18, © The VT323 Project Authors), both under the **SIL Open Font
  License 1.1** (`vendor/fonts/LICENSE`), served as woff2 by
  `vendor/fonts/fonts.css`. The OFL permits redistribution of the font files;
  the Reserved Font Names ("Orbitron", "VT323") mean a *modified* copy must be
  renamed. These are unmodified.
- `vendor/preact/` — **preact 10.19.3** © Jason Miller, **MIT**
  (`vendor/preact/LICENSE`).
- `vendor/htm/` — **htm 3.1.1** © Jason Miller, **Apache-2.0**
  (`vendor/htm/LICENSE`).

Vendoring them is what lets the production Content-Security-Policy say
`default-src 'self'` and what removes the last COEP/CORP question from a
third-party origin (docs/HOSTING.md §1 and "The open-web layer" §4).

